  "body": "## Scope\n\n`research/complex-rank8-rigidity-p106`: a finite verification of a conditional theorem. **No new \u03ba, no\nconstruction, and the selected frontier is unchanged.** It answers the open question of an664's #1560 for\nevery five- and six-line deletion. It supersedes the open questions of #1568.\n\n## Result\n\n#1560's Corollary 2 gives K = D(2G_L)D\u207b\u00b9 for any live set L whose pivot frame satisfies (D), (G), (W) and all\n14 blocks nonempty. This package checks those premises for every unit:\n\n- **P107:** all 1614 orbits of 5-subsets of P112, including the 7 frame-contained ones.\n- **P106:** all 19295 orbits of 6-subsets.\n\nEvery unit has a passing pivot. **So with #1560, every P107 and every P106 unit is rigid.** Through #1212 \u00a78,\nthat gives PR968's floor for masked decoders with exactly eight costly terms: 59 = 72 \u2212 13 at P107 and\n58 = 72 \u2212 14 at P106.\n\nThe route uses none of #1212's Lemmas 5\u20136, #1399's Lemma 9, #1419's Lemma 10, or any DRUP certificate.\n\n**#1560's open question.** Its coverage-failure deletion (3,13,14,22,23) passes at\n(2,5,15,16,30,41,109,116), and at 820 of its 850 live frames.\n\n## Coverage\n\nCoverage extends #1474/#1568's candidate rule to three levels, with explicit generator words:\n\n- 2517 quadruple candidates map onto 180 representatives.\n- 18782 5-subset candidates map onto the 1614 P107 units.\n- 156627 6-subset candidates (a P107 unit plus one line) map onto the 19295 P106 units.\n\nThe verifier replays every word.\n\n## Evidence\n\nThe verifier is stdlib-only, and every check is exact:\n\n- `--level 5` runs 11 checks in 36 s: model, the frame identity (6) on all 2025 frames, generators, triple\n  orbits, the three coverage levels, #1560's fixture and control, a (G)/(D) negative control, a first-frame\n  control, and the 1614 P107 units.\n- `--level 6` checks the 19295 P106 units in 59 s on 10 cores (558 CPU-seconds). The registered replay splits\n  it into two parts.\n- Ranks are computed modulo 1000003, which gives lower bounds; the seven exact kernel vectors give the matching\n  upper bound.\n- The registered replay passes (`PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE ... outcome=completed`), as do Python 3.10\n  and 3.14, and the 20 `tests/test_research_*` tests.\n- `make_units.py` (numpy) regenerates the data. Its census sums the orbit sizes to exactly C(112,5) and\n  C(112,6).\n- A read-only adversarial review by OpenAI Codex found no theorem-breaking issue. It covered the criterion\n  against #1560's definitions, the rank and kernel argument, the coverage induction, and #1560's \u00a74 and \u00a76. Its\n  one low-severity wording point is applied. This is not a human review.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- **#1560's Theorem 1 and Corollary 2** are cited. I read the proof and found no gap, but #1560 is open and has\n  had no independent human review.\n- **Other inherited steps:** #1212's (E), \u00a78 and \u00a710 transport, and PR968's (F6).\n- **P105, and nine or more costly terms.** P105 has 242802 orbits, and the census sizes sum to C(112,7). An\n  unregistered numpy search with float ranks found a passing pivot for every orbit; the first live frame\n  passed for 230560 of them. That search is not exact and is not in this package, because a stdlib replay of\n  that many units exceeds the registered budget. See the open questions.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\n- **Task:** `complex-masked-decoder`, scope refined; see `TASK.json`.\n- **Base:** `ddb4371c`.\n- **Overlap:** #1560 is an664's DONE, and this package uses its criterion with credit. I read #1560 at\n  `5bebfd00`; its current head `eb9f6f15` changes only \u00a77 and \u00a78. #1609 (ToikY) is adjacent but separate: it\n  keeps one factor root-linear and varies an arbitrary deletion count. No other P107 or P106 claim was open as of\n  2026-10-14T04:05Z.\n- **Coordination note:** my claim for this work was misposted to an unrelated repository (since deleted), so\n  there was no claim in 1502 before this PR.\n\n## Credit\n\nan664 / Andrey Mas (#1560), burntout76 / Brett Halligan (#1212), themilkman216 (PR968) and DreamingOfClouds\n(PR717). Prepared with substantial assistance from Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
